==Restrictons==
*Fixed lineup: [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat Mk II]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]].

==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*6 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Scissoroo]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Shy Boy]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss after 90 seconds<sup>2,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage emphasizes the importance of [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]], since the Scissoroos are buffed to the point where they would be very difficult without them. This stage also emphasizes the importance of money management, as cash is going to be very tight, with a limited amount of enemies, and Paris being very heavy on your wallet.

You are provided with a bunch of tankers and meatshields, as well as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] to deal damage. The Alien peons at the beginning are for you to upgrade your worker cat to at least level 3, so spawn a couple Paris Cats to deal with them. [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover Cat]] is not able to tank many hits from even the Alien enemies, so it should generally be avoided. After that, don't upgrade worker any further, since you most likely will run out of money to deal with the Bore if you do. When the Shy Boy spawns, start stacking [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cats]] and Paris Cats, to maximize the damage potential for the upcoming Bore. It should go without saying that the Alien enemies should all be dead by this point. Killing the Shy Boy will fill up your wallet, and the bulk of that money should be utilized to fight the Bore. Spam meatshields, Fried Shrimp cats and Paris cats, while leaving just enough money to continue spawning meatshields, and you should have enough money to kill off the bore and beat the stage.

When Bore comes, just spam Paris Cat, Fried Shrimp Cat, and [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]], just make sure you always have enough money to afford the next Fried Shrimp Cat when it comes off cooldown and you will be fine.

==Hints==
The first hint can be viewed within the Enemies Appearing window before beginning the stage. The second only appears as a defeat message when failing it.
*Speedy and relentless enemies<br>can be held back by deploying <br>Units that are low-cost<br>and have high Vitality
*Stop the enemy's advance by rapidly<br>deploying Mohawk Cat and Eraser Cat.<br>Watch for enemy Traits and respond<br>with Rover Cat Mk II or Fried Shrimp Cat.

